content.content:
- **Layout.** A header with the logo, the title and a dark/light switch (remembered). The left bar
  holds the image (Load, with a dropdown for where from: this computer or Google Drive; a
  thumbnail showing the part in view, which moves the view when clicked; its name; a checkbox per
  colour layer, in that layer's colour when on, blue off at first), the candidates finder (its
  "how it works" and its settings fold away) and the filters. The main area has a toolbar over two
  views: the image and the individual items, with the button that switches between them at its
  left and the zoom at its right. The right bar holds the selected candidate, the
  summary and the downloads. Both side bars can be dragged wider or narrower (remembered; a double
  click restores one). A status bar shows the image name, the candidate and finalist counts, how
  long each step took, and the site's version (stamped by each release).
- **Moving around the image.** Dragging moves the image; scrolling up and down zooms around the
  pointer in small steps; scrolling sideways steps to the previous or next candidate. The Show
  menu switches accepted and rejected markings on and off, each with its own line width and colour,
  and the candidate numbers, the rejection letters and the measuring lines (remembered).
- **One selected candidate.** Clicking a candidate selects it (a thin white ring) and clicking it
  again deselects it. Its card sits in the right bar with buttons to the previous and next
  candidate by number. Decisions are made on cards, not by clicking the image, with two buttons at
  the card's top: Approve (a real NoR, with the lengths shown) and Reject (not one), each saying
  what it does in its tooltip. Approved and rejected-by-user cards have their own border colours,
  and a candidate the user rejected offers Un-reject.
- **Filters are live dials.** Every check in `nor3.CHECKS`, the nucleus rule (N) and
  one-pixel-per-NoR (O) is a control that can be switched off. Each shows a letter, a one- or
  two-word title and a line saying what it means (the page's own names, from
  `detection/finder_help.py`; the lab's review sheets keep theirs), and two counts: how many
  candidates it rejects, whatever the other filters do, and how many only it rejects among the
  filters switched on (what switching it off would let through). Each of its parameters is a
  dial, and every marking on the image follows it at once. A dial moved off our value is marked,
  with our value as a tick on its slider that puts it back. Finder and filter settings use this
  one control, so tweaking looks and works the same in both. A check added to `CHECKS` becomes a control with
  no page change.
- **Detection settings are dials too.** They re-run the finder, and the page says that this takes
  time. Each finder names its main settings (its function's `MAIN`), shown first; every setting is
  under a collapsed Advanced box. Each finder shows a few sentences on how it works, and every setting and
  filter value has a ? that says what it does (`detection/finder_help.py`; the test fails when one
  is missing).
- **All finders are offered.** Traffic light is the default.
- **The blue mask is only a filter.** No finder on the page blanks nuclei before finding.
- **The item views.** Two views: the finalists and the rejected, each candidate cropped on a card:
  its number, state and decision buttons on top, the crop below (with a faint go-to button in its
  corner that shows it on the image), then "Lengths adjusted" with a reset, and the rest.
  A rejected card names every filter that rejects it by itself, or says the user rejected it. An
  Options menu (remembered) sets the crop's context padding, turns each crop so the NoR lies level
  (on at first), and shows or hides the NoR borders, the measurement bars, the lengths on the crop,
  the lengths on the card (off at first) and the length adjusters (on at first). The adjusters drag the ends of
  the green-to-green length and the red length; the new lengths show on the image, the card, the
  summary and the downloads. The measurements of the finalists are summarised in the right bar.
- **Downloads.** The candidates as CSV (every candidate, its status, its reasons, the user's
  decision and its measurements), the summary as CSV, and the ground truth: a JSON file naming the
  image (with its SHA-256) that lists every finalist and every candidate the user decided on, with
  its position, its label (1 = NoR, 0 = not), who decided (the user or the finder), and its
  lengths and length lines, marked as adjusted or approved when the user checked them. The lab's
  `nor_lab.py --labels` reads it: the labels score detection and the checked lengths score
  measurement (`tests/test_ground_truth.py`).
- **Fixed numbers.** Each candidate keeps one number, top to bottom, for as long as a detection
  lasts. Filters never renumber candidates.
- **Remembered marks.** Decisions and adjusted or approved lengths are saved in the browser per
  file name and finder, tied to each candidate's position.
- **Google Drive.** The user pastes the link of an image or a folder shared as "Anyone with the
  link", with no sign-in. An image loads at once; a folder lists its images and subfolders to pick
  from, each image with its size and the date it was added to Drive; the dialog keeps one size
  while the user moves between folders. It needs the site's Google API key, kept in the repository variable `GOOGLE_API_KEY`
  and written into `web/config.js` at deploy; without one the option is off. The dialog opens on
  the last link pasted, or else on the lab's folder (the repository variable
  `DRIVE_DEFAULT_FOLDER`), and lists a folder link at once.
  Nothing read from Drive is cached.

/* a filter: switch, letter, title and its own count on one line, what it means below, then its dials */
.filter { background: var(--bg); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--r-ctl); padding: 10px 12px; margin-bottom: 8px; }
.filter.off .desc, .filter.off .param, .filter.off .title { opacity: .45; }
.filter .top { display: flex; gap: 8px; align-items: center; cursor: pointer; }
.filter .top input { margin: 0; accent-color: var(--accent); }
.filter .badge { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 20px; height: 20px; border-radius: var(--r-chip);
  font-weight: 700; font-size: 12px; border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--c), #000 var(--ink-amt)); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--c) 14%, transparent); }
.filter .title { flex: 1; font-weight: 600; font-size: 13px; }
.filter .n { min-width: 34px; padding: 1px 8px; border-radius: 999px; background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line);
  text-align: center; font-size: 12px; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
.filter .n:empty { display: none; }
.filter .n.only { border-style: dashed; color: var(--dim); }
.filter .desc { color: var(--dim); font-size: 12px; margin: 6px 0 0; }
#overlay.no-pass .pass, #overlay.no-fails .fail, #overlay.no-nums .num, #overlay.no-letters .let { display: none; }
/* the selection: a thin white ring, clear of the markings */
#overlay .ring { fill: none; stroke: #fff; stroke-opacity: .9; stroke-width: 1.25; vector-effect: non-scaling-stroke; pointer-events: none; }
#overlay .lines { display: none; }
#overlay .pass .lines { display: inline; }
#overlay.no-lines .pass .lines { display: none; }
#overlay .lines line { stroke: #fff; vector-effect: non-scaling-stroke; stroke-width: 1; }
#overlay .lines line.r { stroke-width: 2; }
#overlay text { paint-order: stroke; stroke: #000; stroke-width: 2px; stroke-opacity: .6; font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; }
#overlay .hit { fill: transparent; cursor: pointer; }
#overlay g[data-i] { cursor: pointer; }
#overlay .forced path { stroke-dasharray: 2 1; stroke-opacity: 1; }
#overlay .red, #overlay .lines { pointer-events: none; }

#list { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(200px, 1fr)); gap: var(--pad); align-items: start; }
.card { background: var(--bg); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--r-ctl); padding: 10px; font-size: 12px; }
.card .crop { position: relative; width: max-content; max-width: 100%; margin: 0 auto 8px; line-height: 0; }
.card .crop canvas { display: block; image-rendering: pixelated; border-radius: var(--r-chip); max-width: 100%; }
.card .marks { position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; overflow: visible; }
.card .marks line { stroke: #fff; stroke-width: 1; vector-effect: non-scaling-stroke; }
.card .marks line.r { stroke-width: 2.5; }
.card .marks text { fill: #fff; text-anchor: middle; paint-order: stroke; stroke: #000; font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; }
.card .marks text.r { fill: #ffb3b3; }
.card .marks .handle { fill: #fff; stroke: #000; cursor: ew-resize; }
.card .marks .handle.r { fill: #ff6b6b; }
.card .head { display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 8px; }
.card .head .acts { margin-left: auto; display: flex; gap: 4px; }
.card .head .acts button { padding: 1px 6px; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.3; background: var(--panel); }
.card .head .acts button.emoji { filter: grayscale(1); opacity: .7; }
.card .head .acts button.emoji:hover, .card .head .acts button.emoji.on { filter: none; opacity: 1; }
.card .head .acts button.on { border-color: #2fb344; }
.card .head .acts button.text { font-size: 11px; }
/* the go-to button sits on the crop, faint until the pointer is over it */
.card .crop-wrap { position: relative; width: max-content; max-width: 100%; margin: 0 auto 8px; }
.card .crop-wrap .crop { margin: 0; }
.card .goto { position: absolute; top: 5px; right: 5px; width: 26px; height: 26px; padding: 0; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
  border-radius: 50%; border: 1px solid #ffffff60; background: #000000a0; color: #fff; opacity: .3; transition: opacity .15s; }
.card .crop-wrap:hover .goto, .card .goto:focus-visible { opacity: 1; }
.card .goto:hover { background: var(--accent); border-color: var(--accent); }
.card .goto svg { fill: none; stroke: currentColor; stroke-width: 2; stroke-linecap: round; }
.card .goto svg .dot { fill: currentColor; stroke: none; }
.card .num { font-weight: 700; }
.card.pass .num { color: var(--pink); } .card.fail .num { color: var(--blue); }
.card .state { color: var(--dim); }
.card .tag { color: var(--warn); margin: -2px 0 4px; }
.card .why { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 4px 10px; margin: 2px 0 6px; }
.card.approved { border-color: #2fb344; }
.card.byyou { border-color: var(--warn); }
.card .tag button { font-size: 12px; margin-left: 6px; }
.card button { padding: 2px 8px; font-size: 11px; border-radius: var(--r-chip); }
.card table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; }
.card td:last-child { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
.card td { color: var(--dim); } .card td:last-child { color: var(--text); }

#selected .card { background: var(--bg); }
.stepper { display: inline-flex; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--r-ctl); overflow: hidden; }
.stepper button { border: 0; border-radius: 0; background: transparent; width: 32px; padding: 2px 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.2; }
.stepper button + button { border-left: 1px solid var(--line); }
.stepper button:not(:disabled):hover { background: var(--bg); }
#selected-box .sec-head { margin-bottom: 10px; }
#downloads { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; align-items: center; }
#downloads h2 { flex-basis: 100%; margin-bottom: 2px; }
#summary .tbl { overflow-x: auto; }
#summary table { border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: 8px; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; font-size: 12px; width: 100%; }
#summary th, #summary td { padding: 4px 4px; text-align: right; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
#summary th:first-child, #summary td:first-child { text-align: left; }
#summary .hists { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; margin-top: 12px; }
#summary .hist { font-size: 12px; color: var(--dim); }
#summary .hist rect { fill: var(--pink); opacity: .75; }
#summary .reasons { margin-top: 12px; color: var(--dim); font-size: 13px; }

/* the footer: file, counts and timings as sections on the left; progress and the version on the right */
#statusbar { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; height: 1cm; padding: 0 14px; background: var(--panel); border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  font-size: 12px; color: var(--dim); white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; }
#statusbar .seg { padding-right: 10px; border-right: 1px solid var(--line); }
#statusbar .seg:empty { display: none; }
#statusbar .grow { flex: 1; }
#statusbar b { color: var(--text); font-weight: 600; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
#sb-file { color: var(--text); font-weight: 600; max-width: 30vw; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; }
#sb-times { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
#status { overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; min-width: 0; }
#status.err { color: var(--err); }
#statusbar .spin { width: 12px; height: 12px; display: none; }
#statusbar .spin.on { display: inline-block; }
#sb-version { padding: 1px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--r-chip); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
#sb-version.stale { cursor: pointer; color: var(--bg); background: var(--warn); border-color: var(--warn); font-weight: 600; }

#tip { position: fixed; pointer-events: none; background: var(--tipbg); color: var(--text); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--r-ctl); padding: 8px 10px; font-size: 12px; max-width: 320px; z-index: 10; white-space: pre-line; }

@media (max-width: 1300px) {
  #layout { --lw: 260px; --rw: 300px; }
}

.spin { display: inline-block; width: 14px; height: 14px; border: 2px solid var(--line); border-top-color: var(--pink); border-radius: 50%; animation: spin .8s linear infinite; visibility: hidden; }
.spin.on { visibility: visible; }
.spin.big { width: 44px; height: 44px; border-width: 4px; visibility: visible; }
@keyframes spin { to { transform: rotate(360deg); } }
#busy { position: absolute; inset: 52px 0 0 0; z-index: 5; display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 10px; background: var(--shade); color: var(--text); }
#busy[hidden] { display: none; }
#busy-time { color: var(--dim); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
/* over an image (Find Candidates, or one painting as it downloads) the text sits in a pill below it, and
   Find Candidates sweeps a copier's light bar back and forth over the image */
#scan-light { display: none; }
#busy.scan, #busy.peek { background: none; justify-content: flex-end; padding-bottom: 28px; pointer-events: none; overflow: hidden; }
#busy.scan .spin.big, #busy.peek .spin.big { display: none; }
#busy.scan #busy-text, #busy.scan #busy-time, #busy.peek #busy-text, #busy.peek #busy-time { position: relative; z-index: 1; }
#busy.scan #busy-text, #busy.peek #busy-text { padding: 5px 14px; border-radius: 999px; background: var(--shade); font-weight: 600; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
#busy.scan #busy-time, #busy.peek #busy-time { margin-top: -6px; padding: 1px 10px; border-radius: 999px; background: var(--shade); color: var(--text); }
#busy.scan #scan-light { display: block; position: absolute; top: 0; bottom: 0; left: -90px; width: 90px; mix-blend-mode: screen;
  background: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, rgba(150, 255, 190, .10) 30%, rgba(235, 255, 245, .75) 50%, rgba(150, 255, 190, .10) 70%, transparent);
  box-shadow: 0 0 60px 20px rgba(120, 255, 170, .18); animation: copier 2.4s ease-in-out infinite alternate; }
@keyframes copier { from { transform: translateX(0); } to { transform: translateX(calc(100cqw + 90px)); } }
#busy.scan { container-type: inline-size; }
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { #busy.scan #scan-light { animation-duration: 8s; } }

/* the Google Drive dialog */
#drive-dlg { width: min(640px, calc(100vw - 32px)); padding: 18px; color: var(--text); background: var(--panel);
  border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--r-panel); box-shadow: 0 12px 40px #0006; }
#drive-dlg::backdrop { background: #0007; }
.drive-row { display: flex; gap: 8px; align-items: center; margin-top: 10px; }
.drive-row.end { justify-content: space-between; }
#drive-link { flex: 1; min-width: 0; }
/* every part keeps its size whatever the folder holds, so the dialog stays still while browsing */
#drive-path { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 13px; height: 1.5em; line-height: 1.5em; white-space: nowrap; overflow-x: auto; overflow-y: hidden; }
#drive-list { display: flex; flex-direction: column; height: 300px; overflow-y: auto; margin-top: 6px;
  border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--r-ctl); }
#drive-list .item { display: flex; gap: 12px; align-items: baseline; flex: none; text-align: left; border: 0; border-radius: 0; background: none; padding: 6px 10px; }
#drive-list .item .name { flex: 1; min-width: 0; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
#drive-list .item .meta { color: var(--dim); font-size: 12px; white-space: nowrap; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
#drive-msg { flex: 1; min-width: 0; white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; }
#drive-list .item + .item { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
#drive-list .item:hover { background: var(--bg); }
#drive-list .item.folder .name::before { content: "📁 "; }
#drive-msg.err { color: var(--err); }

/* a box that folds: its title opens and closes it */
.box.foldable > .sec-head h2 { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 7px; cursor: pointer; user-select: none; }
.box.foldable > .sec-head h2::before { content: ""; border: 5px solid transparent; border-top: 6px solid var(--dim); border-bottom: 0; transition: transform .15s; }
.box.foldable.folded > .sec-head h2::before { transform: rotate(-90deg); }
.box.foldable.folded > :not(.sec-head) { display: none; }
.box.foldable.folded > .sec-head button { display: none; }

toolUseResult.stdout:
- **Layout.** A header with the logo, the title and a dark/light switch (remembered). The left bar
  holds the image (Load, with a dropdown for where from: this computer or Google Drive; a
  thumbnail showing the part in view, which moves the view when clicked; its name; a checkbox per
  colour layer, in that layer's colour when on, blue off at first), the candidates finder (its
  "how it works" and its settings fold away) and the filters. The main area has a toolbar over two
  views: the image and the individual items, with the button that switches between them at its
  left and the zoom at its right. The right bar holds the selected candidate, the
  summary and the downloads. Both side bars can be dragged wider or narrower (remembered; a double
  click restores one). A status bar shows the image name, the candidate and finalist counts, how
  long each step took, and the site's version (stamped by each release).
- **Moving around the image.** Dragging moves the image; scrolling up and down zooms around the
  pointer in small steps; scrolling sideways steps to the previous or next candidate. The Show
  menu switches accepted and rejected markings on and off, each with its own line width and colour,
  and the candidate numbers, the rejection letters and the measuring lines (remembered).
- **One selected candidate.** Clicking a candidate selects it (a thin white ring) and clicking it
  again deselects it. Its card sits in the right bar with buttons to the previous and next
  candidate by number. Decisions are made on cards, not by clicking the image, with two buttons at
  the card's top: Approve (a real NoR, with the lengths shown) and Reject (not one), each saying
  what it does in its tooltip. Approved and rejected-by-user cards have their own border colours,
  and a candidate the user rejected offers Un-reject.
- **Filters are live dials.** Every check in `nor3.CHECKS`, the nucleus rule (N) and
  one-pixel-per-NoR (O) is a control that can be switched off. Each shows a letter, a one- or
  two-word title and a line saying what it means (the page's own names, from
  `detection/finder_help.py`; the lab's review sheets keep theirs), and two counts: how many
  candidates it rejects, whatever the other filters do, and how many only it rejects among the
  filters switched on (what switching it off would let through). Each of its parameters is a
  dial, and every marking on the image follows it at once. A dial moved off our value is marked,
  with our value as a tick on its slider that puts it back. Finder and filter settings use this
  one control, so tweaking looks and works the same in both. A check added to `CHECKS` becomes a control with
  no page change.
- **Detection settings are dials too.** They re-run the finder, and the page says that this takes
  time. Each finder names its main settings (its function's `MAIN`), shown first; every setting is
  under a collapsed Advanced box. Each finder shows a few sentences on how it works, and every setting and
  filter value has a ? that says what it does (`detection/finder_help.py`; the test fails when one
  is missing).
- **All finders are offered.** Traffic light is the default.
- **The blue mask is only a filter.** No finder on the page blanks nuclei before finding.
- **The item views.** Two views: the finalists and the rejected, each candidate cropped on a card:
  its number, state and decision buttons on top, the crop below (with a faint go-to button in its
  corner that shows it on the image), then "Lengths adjusted" with a reset, and the rest.
  A rejected card names every filter that rejects it by itself, or says the user rejected it. An
  Options menu (remembered) sets the crop's context padding, turns each crop so the NoR lies level
  (on at first), and shows or hides the NoR borders, the measurement bars, the lengths on the crop,
  the lengths on the card (off at first) and the length adjusters (on at first). The adjusters drag the ends of
  the green-to-green length and the red length; the new lengths show on the image, the card, the
  summary and the downloads. The measurements of the finalists are summarised in the right bar.
- **Downloads.** The candidates as CSV (every candidate, its status, its reasons, the user's
  decision and its measurements), the summary as CSV, and the ground truth: a JSON file naming the
  image (with its SHA-256) that lists every finalist and every candidate the user decided on, with
  its position, its label (1 = NoR, 0 = not), who decided (the user or the finder), and its
  lengths and length lines, marked as adjusted or approved when the user checked them. The lab's
  `nor_lab.py --labels` reads it: the labels score detection and the checked lengths score
  measurement (`tests/test_ground_truth.py`).
- **Fixed numbers.** Each candidate keeps one number, top to bottom, for as long as a detection
  lasts. Filters never renumber candidates.
- **Remembered marks.** Decisions and adjusted or approved lengths are saved in the browser per
  file name and finder, tied to each candidate's position.
- **Google Drive.** The user pastes the link of an image or a folder shared as "Anyone with the
  link", with no sign-in. An image loads at once; a folder lists its images and subfolders to pick
  from, each image with its size and the date it was added to Drive; the dialog keeps one size
  while the user moves between folders. It needs the site's Google API key, kept in the repository variable `GOOGLE_API_KEY`
  and written into `web/config.js` at deploy; without one the option is off. The dialog opens on
  the last link pasted, or else on the lab's folder (the repository variable
  `DRIVE_DEFAULT_FOLDER`), and lists a folder link at once.
  Nothing read from Drive is cached.

/* a filter: switch, letter, title and its own count on one line, what it means below, then its dials */
.filter { background: var(--bg); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--r-ctl); padding: 10px 12px; margin-bottom: 8px; }
.filter.off .desc, .filter.off .param, .filter.off .title { opacity: .45; }
.filter .top { display: flex; gap: 8px; align-items: center; cursor: pointer; }
.filter .top input { margin: 0; accent-color: var(--accent); }
.filter .badge { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 20px; height: 20px; border-radius: var(--r-chip);
  font-weight: 700; font-size: 12px; border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--c), #000 var(--ink-amt)); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--c) 14%, transparent); }
.filter .title { flex: 1; font-weight: 600; font-size: 13px; }
.filter .n { min-width: 34px; padding: 1px 8px; border-radius: 999px; background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line);
  text-align: center; font-size: 12px; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
.filter .n:empty { display: none; }
.filter .n.only { border-style: dashed; color: var(--dim); }
.filter .desc { color: var(--dim); font-size: 12px; margin: 6px 0 0; }
#overlay.no-pass .pass, #overlay.no-fails .fail, #overlay.no-nums .num, #overlay.no-letters .let { display: none; }
/* the selection: a thin white ring, clear of the markings */
#overlay .ring { fill: none; stroke: #fff; stroke-opacity: .9; stroke-width: 1.25; vector-effect: non-scaling-stroke; pointer-events: none; }
#overlay .lines { display: none; }
#overlay .pass .lines { display: inline; }
#overlay.no-lines .pass .lines { display: none; }
#overlay .lines line { stroke: #fff; vector-effect: non-scaling-stroke; stroke-width: 1; }
#overlay .lines line.r { stroke-width: 2; }
#overlay text { paint-order: stroke; stroke: #000; stroke-width: 2px; stroke-opacity: .6; font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; }
#overlay .hit { fill: transparent; cursor: pointer; }
#overlay g[data-i] { cursor: pointer; }
#overlay .forced path { stroke-dasharray: 2 1; stroke-opacity: 1; }
#overlay .red, #overlay .lines { pointer-events: none; }

